<%# One reading measure for the long legal texts (owner's repair request of
    2026-10-21, item 4). A judgment's and a parliamentary document's full text
    stayed justified on a 390 px phone, where a line holds too few words to
    spread and the gaps stretch. They now justify only from 40rem, and
    hyphenate in the language of the text (the container carries its lang). A
    law's articles only stop justifying on a phone. No text-align-last: it is
    inherited, and set on the container it pulled every centred one-line child
    (the judgment's masthead) to the start; a justified paragraph's last line
    starts naturally without it. These rules are unlayered, so they win over
    the stylesheet's @layer base without an asset build.
    The width (owner's requirement of 2026-11-07, via Sol 08:17:34Z): a
    judgment, a parliamentary document and a law's text read at the full width
    of their card unless the reader chose Wide (64rem) or Comfortable (80
    characters), centred (reading_width_controller.js). Full is also the width
    without JavaScript and before a saved choice arrives. The heading row above
    a judgment's or parliamentary document's text takes the same measure (Sol,
    on live 1.1.24, 06:57:39Z). The choice shows from 48rem, with JavaScript. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
<style>
  .reading-body {
    text-align: start;
    hyphens: auto;
    -webkit-hyphens: auto;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }
  .reading-measure { margin-inline: auto; }
  .reading-measure[data-reading-width="wide"] { max-width: min(100%, 64rem); }
  .reading-measure[data-reading-width="comfortable"] { max-width: min(100%, 80ch); }
  /* A judgment's list the source writes with dashes keeps them (ParliamentaryHelper, Sol 08:17:34Z). */
  .reading-body ul[data-list-marker="dash"] { list-style-type: "3  "; }
  .article-content { text-align: start; }
  .reading-width-control { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .reading-body,
    .article-content {
      text-align: justify;
      text-justify: inter-word;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .reading-width-control:not([hidden]) { display: inline-flex; }
  }
</style>
<% end %>
